 :problem
 {:source "オーナー指示 2026-07-07: 「では設計実装してください. maps, search なども datomic 系をベースに.」"
  :facts
  ["net-kotobase had datomic.*/graph.*/kg.* query families but zero
    webpage-search or maps surface (verified 2026-07-07 against lexicons,
    worker routes, and docs)."
   "kg.search is ontology/entity-shaped (OWL classes, embeddings), not a
    page or place surface."]}

 :decision
 {:nsids
  {:web.ingest "caller-extracted {url,title,text,lang} -> :webpage/* datoms via the tenant-cap datomic.transact CACAO gate (graph kotobase/db/<did>/<db_name>, default webpages). Edge does not crawl (no SSRF)."
   :web.search "one :limit-1000-capped map-form datomic.q scan + edge ranking: ASCII + CJK-bigram tokens (Japanese without a segmenter), coverage-dominant deterministic score (title x3, capped tf), snippets."
   :geo.ingest "{name,lat,lon,id?,tags?} -> :place/* datoms, same gate, default graph places; id slugged deterministically from name when absent."
   :geo.search "same capped datomic.q scan + edge-side bbox containment or haversine radius (distance_m ranking); exactly one of bbox|near required."}
  :invariants
  ["No new pod surface, storage, or auth model -- everything compiles onto the existing datomic.* plane"
   "Ingest reuses proxy/authorize-tenant-cap-write unchanged (client graph CID cannot override ownership)"
   "Generated Datalog is data-patterns-only; pod predicate/fulltext push-down is a follow-up lift (kotoba-datomic support unverified); the candidates response field makes the 1000-row recall cap observable"
   "Clojure stays schema authority: webpages/places join kotobase.schema well-known; :webpage/url and :place/id are :db.unique/identity; datomic.listDatabases advertises 4 graphs"]
  :artifacts
  ["clj-edge/src/kotobase/{web,geo,rows,domain_search}.cljc (pure cores + cljs route glue)"
   "contracts/lexicons/ai/gftd/apps/kotobase/{web,geo}/{ingest,search}.json"
   "worker/test/web_geo_search_test.cljc (against the rebuilt committed bundle, 8/8)"
   "docs/adr/2607072330-web-geo-datalog-search.md (in-repo detail)"]}

